{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And it shall be, that good thing.</b> What good did they do for him? They said: when Israel were dividing the land, the fenced-off area of Jericho was five hundred cubits by five hundred cubits, and they set it aside from division, saying: whoever builds the Temple in his portion — he shall take it. And in the meantime they gave it to the descendants of Yitro, to Yonadav ben Rechav, as it is said: ״וּבְנֵי קֵינִי חֹתֵן מֹשֶׁה עָלוּ מֵעִיר הַתְּמָרִים״ and so forth (Judges 1)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:15.653481306Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}